WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.240
So you've got a video in your app, but you want AI to actually do something

2
00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:04.720
with it,

3
00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:08.880
like generating chapters, moderating your uploads, creating translations, and

4
00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:09.360
more.

5
00:00:09.360 --> 00:00:13.360
Normally, that means you have to stitch together third-party services, building

6
00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:14.160
job queues,

7
00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:18.400
and then also creating custom glue code. With the Mux Robots API, you can skip

8
00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:19.040
all of that.

9
00:00:19.040 --> 00:00:24.240
Robots is a job-based API that runs AI workflows on your Mux assets.

10
00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:27.440
And it's pretty simple. You send an HTTP request to create a

11
00:00:27.440 --> 00:00:31.360
Robots job, and Mux processes that video with that AI workflow.

12
00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:35.070
And you get a structure result back with one API call, or you can use the

13
00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:35.520
dashboard.

14
00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:38.720
So let's look at a few of these workflows, starting with summarization.

15
00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:42.640
When you fire off a summarization job, Mux Robots will give you back a title,

16
00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:47.200
a description, and an array of tags. Some other parameters you can control are

17
00:00:47.200 --> 00:00:47.920
the tone,

18
00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:51.280
so you can change the tone from playful, professional, or neutral.

19
00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:54.480
You can set word limitations for the title and description.

20
00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:57.840
And on top of that, you can also override sections of the prompt as well.

21
00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:02.000
The moderation job samples the frames of your video and moderates each one

22
00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:02.880
frame-by-frame.

23
00:01:02.880 --> 00:01:06.480
You can also set your threshold. The lower the threshold, the stricter the

24
00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:07.520
moderation will be.

25
00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:11.360
And the higher the threshold, the more permissive the model and the moderation

26
00:01:11.360 --> 00:01:12.320
jobs will be as well.

27
00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:14.720
The asked questions job might be the most underrated.

28
00:01:14.720 --> 00:01:17.540
It's actually a lot more powerful than you think, and it's a bit of a Swiss

29
00:01:17.540 --> 00:01:18.320
Army knife.

30
00:01:18.320 --> 00:01:22.260
You can ask a question or a bunch of questions, and you get back a structured

31
00:01:22.260 --> 00:01:22.800
answer.

32
00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:26.740
You also get the confidence score and the reasoning of why that confidence

33
00:01:26.740 --> 00:01:27.440
score was given.

34
00:01:27.440 --> 00:01:30.960
You can use the ask questions job to classify your uploads.

35
00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:35.240
You can route your content and also build decision logic all without training a

36
00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:35.600
model.

37
00:01:35.600 --> 00:01:38.960
The generating chapters job takes analyzation to the next step,

38
00:01:38.960 --> 00:01:43.440
where Mux Robots analyzes your assets caption track to create timestamp

39
00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:44.080
chapters.

40
00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:48.080
When a generating chapters job is completed, you get back an array with the

41
00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:48.800
start time

42
00:01:48.800 --> 00:01:52.960
and also the title of the chapters, which is really good for long-form content.

43
00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:55.880
And if you want to add some customization, you can also change the chapter

44
00:01:55.880 --> 00:01:56.320
density

45
00:01:56.320 --> 00:01:58.800
and the title style by doing a prompt override.

46
00:01:58.800 --> 00:02:01.920
Sifting through a video to find the best moments could take some time.

47
00:02:01.920 --> 00:02:05.200
But with Mux Robots, you also have the Find Key Moments API.

48
00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:08.880
The Find Key Moments job does an audio and visual analyzation

49
00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:12.240
that can help you find the most compelling segments in a video.

50
00:02:12.240 --> 00:02:15.040
Each key moment also comes back with a quality score,

51
00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:18.800
a short title, and a description of what's happening in that key moment.

52
00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:22.800
I can see this job being heavily used for creating highlights from sports games

53
00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:22.800
,

54
00:02:22.800 --> 00:02:25.440
doing social media clips, or previewing content.

55
00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:27.840
The translating captions job is pretty straightforward.

56
00:02:27.840 --> 00:02:31.360
You have your source language, the target language, and your asset ID.

57
00:02:31.360 --> 00:02:34.880
This job will automatically translate an existing caption track

58
00:02:34.880 --> 00:02:37.840
and attach it to your asset with no extra steps.

59
00:02:37.840 --> 00:02:41.600
And lastly, Mux Robots also has jobs to help you manage all of your jobs

60
00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:47.070
across all AI workflows, so you can list, retrieve, or cancel jobs with one API

61
00:02:47.070 --> 00:02:47.520
call.

62
00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:51.920
And that's Mux Robots, a bunch of AI workflows, and one consistent interface.
